Subject: KMSDRM: Restore an originally disabled CRTC as disabled

The saved CRTC may have no framebuffer or valid mode. SDL selects a
preferred mode for its own window in that case, but that fallback is not
the display state to restore. Passing it together with the saved zero
framebuffer asks KMS to enable a nonexistent framebuffer; the retry repeats
the same invalid request.

Choose the restore request from the saved mode_valid flag. Keep the enabled
restore path unchanged; for an originally disabled CRTC use no framebuffer,
connectors or mode. Preserve SDL_LogError for genuine restore failures.

This is a generic KMSDRM correction with no platform or application checks.
Prepared against SDL 2.32.10; not submitted or accepted upstream. The source
regression control is documented in ../test/README.md. Maintainer exception:
docs/graphics/compatibility-v1.md, D-60.

--- a/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmvideo.c
+++ b/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmvideo.c
@@ -1097,15 +1097,16 @@
     /* original video mode and make it point to the original TTY buffer.   */
     /***********************************************************************/
 
-    ret = KMSDRM_drmModeSetCrtc(viddata->drm_fd, dispdata->crtc->crtc_id,
-                                dispdata->crtc->buffer_id, 0, 0, &dispdata->connector->connector_id, 1,
-                                &dispdata->original_mode);
-
-    /* If we failed to set the original mode, try to set the connector prefered mode. */
-    if (ret && (dispdata->crtc->mode_valid == 0)) {
+    /* original_mode may be the preferred mode selected for SDL when the
+       saved CRTC was disabled. Passing it with buffer_id 0 asks KMS to enable
+       a nonexistent framebuffer; restore the saved disabled state instead. */
+    if (dispdata->crtc->mode_valid) {
         ret = KMSDRM_drmModeSetCrtc(viddata->drm_fd, dispdata->crtc->crtc_id,
                                     dispdata->crtc->buffer_id, 0, 0, &dispdata->connector->connector_id, 1,
                                     &dispdata->original_mode);
+    } else {
+        ret = KMSDRM_drmModeSetCrtc(viddata->drm_fd, dispdata->crtc->crtc_id,
+                                    0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL);
     }
 
     if (ret) {
